# ADR-005: Code Quality Tooling

## Status

Accepted

## Context

{{.ServiceName}} needs automated code quality checks to maintain consistency across the team.

## Decision
{{- if .HasGolangCILint}}

### golangci-lint
Configured in `.golangci.yaml` with curated linter set. Run before every commit and in CI.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasGofumpt}}

### gofumpt
Stricter formatting than standard `gofmt`. Enforces consistent code style.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasPreCommitHook}}

### Pre-commit Hook
Runs linting and formatting checks before each commit to catch issues early.
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasCommitMsgHook}}

### Conventional Commits
Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format, enforced by a commit-msg hook.
{{- end}}

## Consequences

- Code quality is enforced automatically, reducing review burden
{{- if .HasPreCommitHook}}
- Pre-commit hooks may slow down commits slightly but prevent CI failures
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasCommitMsgHook}}
- Conventional commits enable automated changelog generation
{{- end}}

